            "type": "string"
          },
          "created_at": {
            "title": "Created At",
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "expires_at": {
            "title": "Expires At",
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "created_by": {
            "title": "Created By",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "revoked_at": {
            "title": "Revoked At",
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "last_used_at": {
            "title": "Last Used At",
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time"
          }
        },
        "description": "Information about an API key that is safe to return to users\n\nSecurity Design:\n- API key tokens are sensitive authentication credentials (like passwords)\n- Unlike resource IDs (project_id, cloud_id), API key tokens can be used directly for authentication\n- Therefore, we never expose the full token to the frontend to prevent token theft\n\nImplementation:\n- hex_hashed_id: Contains hex_hashed_id (Blake2B hash of the actual token) for secure revoke operations\n- display_id: Contains only the last 6 characters of the actual token for user identification\n- Security relies on backend user isolation: all operations must check user_id/organization_id"
      },
